Whereas I always take mine, if possible. Sokoban has
gotten so easy for me with hundreds of repeated
visits, I need the challenge of navigating around
pets to keep my interest up. This is especially fun
if you don't have, or don't use, telepathy. Plus,
slowing down to make sure all pets are accounted for
before taking a move ups my survival rate
tremendously over my usual "type too fast to notice
that your PC is dying" mode.

I invented a "new to me" trick that works well with
pets in Sokoban; I really don't want them between me
with my boulder, and the hole or pit I'm trying to
fill.  It turns out that if you drop something
cursed at the point where entry to the passage with
the holes/pits is narrow, pets tend much more
strongly to stay out of there, preferring strongly
not to walk across the cursed object.

I'm going to generalize that in the future to use
cursed objects as cat herding tools elsewhere in the
dungeon.

